      <item row="5" column="1">
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="cinematicModeComboBox">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Off: surface shading only, lit by the standard five-light rig. The depth settings switch the 3D window to a key light with a dimmer opposing fill, and trace short shadow rays through the volume so that contacts and recesses darken; surface shading and its highlight stay on top of that. The rays are kept short on purpose - long ones let one structure cast onto another, which describes the lighting rather than the anatomy. The three settings differ only in how much of the shading the occlusion accounts for. All of them cost more per frame in a still image, are switched off while you drag, and relight any surface in the same window.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
